{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]The [D]king ordered [D/F#]Ashpenaz the [G]chief of his [A]court officials
[D]To bring [D/F#]in some of the Is[G]raelites from [A]the royal family
[D]Young men without any [D/F#]physical [G]defect and [A]handsome
[D]Skilled in all [D/F#]wisdom and en[G]dowed with [A]knowledge
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[G]Fit to serve in the king's [A]palace
To learn the [D]writing and the [Dmaj7/F#]language of [G]the Chaldeans
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D]Ashpenaz [D/F#]gave them [G]new Babylonian [A]names
[D]Belteshazzar [D/F#]Shadrach Me[G]shach and Abedne[A]go
But [Bm]Daniel re[Dmaj7/A]solved in his [G]heart
Not to defi[Em]le himself with the king's [A]food [D][D/F#][G][A]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]God granted him [D/F#]favor and compas[G]sion
In the [A]sight of the chief offi[D]cial
Yet [D/F#]Ashpe[G]naz feared the lord [A]the king
Who [D]assigned [D/F#]their food [G]and drink
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Afraid [D]the king would [D/F#]see them looking worse
[G]Than the other young [A]men [D]their age
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Ashpe[D/F#]naz gave them [G]new Babylonian [A]names
[D]Belteshazzar [D/F#]Shadrach Me[G]shach and Abedne[A]go
But [Bm]Daniel re[Dmaj7/A]solved in his [G]heart
Not to defi[Em7]le himself with the king's [A]food
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
